# Mechanism: from-installer — vendor install script (HTTPS) → PATH binary.
# Format: <detect-binary>  <installer-url>  <pin>  [interp=bash|sh]  [os=mac,linux]  [args=...]
#
# THE PIN IS MANDATORY, and it is one of three things (081M25Z29W4087G0R002Y0Q1MG):
#
#   sha256=<64-hex>                     the bytes are verified before the script is EXECUTED,
#                                       and a mismatch means it is never spawned.
#   sha256=tag-only  tagonly=<reason>   the URL carries a version-shaped tag and we pin the tag
#                                       instead of the digest.
#   sha256=unpinned  unpinned=<reason>  the endpoint has no version at all. The weakest claim,
#                                       and it is REFUSED on a URL that does have a version tag.
#
# The reason is a VALUE, never a comment: a comment is copied along with the line it excuses.
# Same vocabulary as from-url / from-elan / from-autotools-tarball — see
# `src/Core.TypeScript/ace/setup-realizers/unhashed-pin.ts`. Every declared row appears in
# `docs/UNHASHED-DEPENDENCIES.md`, which is derived, not hand-kept.
#
# WHAT THIS MECHANISM DOES, said plainly, because it is why the declaration matters most here:
# it downloads a shell script over HTTPS and runs it with the operator's privileges. Until
# 2026-09-10 there was no digest slot in this format, so all six rows below were unverified and
# nothing in the tree recorded that. They are unverified still — vendor CLIs publish no stable
# artifact — but the exposure is now declared, counted, and printed at install time instead of
# being the silent default.
#
# Best-effort dev CLIs; non-interactive runs skip unless ZETA_INSTALL_FULL=1.

grok          https://x.ai/cli/install.sh                                                            sha256=unpinned  unpinned=xai-serves-one-unversioned-install-endpoint-and-publishes-no-release-artifact
cursor-agent  https://cursor.com/install                                                             sha256=unpinned  unpinned=cursor-publishes-a-single-rolling-install-endpoint-with-no-version-in-the-path
kiro-cli      https://cli.kiro.dev/install                                                           sha256=unpinned  unpinned=kiro-cli-endpoint-is-unversioned-and-upstream-publishes-no-tagged-installer    os=mac
hermes        https://raw.githubusercontent.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent/main/scripts/install.sh    sha256=unpinned  unpinned=installer-is-served-from-the-main-branch-so-there-is-no-tag-and-no-stable-digest    args=--skip-setup
forge         https://forgecode.dev/cli                                                              sha256=unpinned  unpinned=forgecode-serves-one-rolling-cli-endpoint-with-no-versioned-path    interp=sh
agy           https://antigravity.google/cli/install.sh                                              sha256=unpinned  unpinned=antigravity-serves-one-unversioned-install-endpoint-per-release-channel
